To create a user-friendly rating system with emojis using JavaScript for a website's products, you can follow these steps:

1. Create an HTML structure for the rating system that includes the emojis and their corresponding meanings.

```html
<div class="rating-system">
  <button class="emoji emoji-1" data-emoji="1">😃</button>
  <button class="emoji emoji-2" data-emoji="2">😐</button>
  <button class="emoji emoji-3" data-emoji="3">😔</button>
  <button class="emoji emoji-4" data-emoji="4">😠</button>
  <button class="emoji emoji-5" data-emoji="5">😢</button>
</div>
```

2. Add CSS styles to highlight the chosen emoji and make the rating system look visually appealing.

```css
.rating-system {
  display: flex;
  justify-content: center;
  align-items: center;
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
}

.emoji {
  width: 50px;
  height: 50px;
  border-radius: 50%;
  background-color: #f5f5f5;
  cursor: pointer;
  transition: background-color 0.3s;
}

.emoji:hover {
  background-color: #e5e5e5;
}

.emoji.active {
  background-color: #4caf50;
  color: #fff;
}
```

3. Add JavaScript code to handle the user's click event and save the chosen emoji.

```javascript
const emojis = document.querySelectorAll('.emoji');

emojis.forEach(emoji => {
  emoji.addEventListener('click', () => {
    emojis.forEach(e => e.classList.remove('active'));
    emoji.classList.add('active');
    saveEmoji(emoji.dataset.emoji);
  });
});

function saveEmoji(emoji) {
  // Save the chosen emoji to the database
  // You can use localStorage or any other storage solution
  localStorage.setItem('productEmoji', emoji);
}
```

4. Display the user's chosen emoji alongside the product for future users to see.

```javascript
const productEmoji = localStorage.getItem('productEmoji');

if (productEmoji) {
  const productEmojiElement = document.createElement('span');
  productEmojiElement.textContent = productEmoji;
  productEmojiElement.classList.add('product-emoji');
  productElement.appendChild(productEmojiElement);
}
```

This rating system allows users to rate products based on their personal experience using emojis, saves the user's chosen emoji, and displays it alongside the product for future users to see. The rating system is user-friendly and visually appealing, making it easy for users to click on the emoji that best represents their experience with the product.

In this example, I will show you how to download images from a specified URL using the LWP::UserAgent and Image::Magick modules in Perl. This program will download all the images from a given URL and save them in the current directory.

```perl
#!/usr/bin/perl

use strict;
use warnings;

use LWP::UserAgent;
use Image::Magick;

# Check if URL is provided
if (@ARGV != 1) {
    print "Usage: $0 <URL>\n";
    exit;
}

my $url = $ARGV[0];

# Initialize LWP user agent
my $ua = LWP::UserAgent->new;

# Fetch the HTML content
my $html = $ua->get($url);

# Check for errors
if ($html->is_error) {
    print "Error fetching URL: " . $html->status_line . "\n";
    exit;
}

# Parse HTML to get image URLs
my @image_urls = $html->find_all_urls({ type => 'image' });

# Download and save images
foreach my $image_url (@image_urls) {
    my $image = $ua->get($image_url);

    if ($image->is_error) {
        print "Error downloading image: " . $image->status_line . "\n";
        next;
    }

    my $filename = $image_url =~ /\/(.*?)\./;
    $filename =~ s/[^a-zA-Z0-9]/_/g;

    Image::Magick->new->read($image->content);
    $Image::Magick->Write($filename, $Image::Magick->Get);

    print "Downloaded image: $filename\n";
}
```

To use this program, save it to a file called `download_images.pl` and run it with the following command:

```bash
perl download_images.pl <URL>
```

Replace `<URL>` with the URL containing the images you want to download.

Please note that this is just an example and should not be used as-is in production. You should add error handling and validation to make sure the program works correctly and securely. Also, make sure to install the required Perl modules using CPAN or your system's package manager.

Happy coding! 😊
